{
  "name": "Afro-Bench Holdout",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "createdAt": "2026-07-26",
  "purpose": "The number we are allowed to believe. Afro-Bench itself has become partly in-sample: lexicon entries were written after reading its failures, so its score now measures the lexicon's coverage of that set as much as the router's understanding. This file is the control — prompts written to be answered by nobody, never consulted while tuning.",
  "rules": [
    "NEVER add a lexicon phrase, manifest synonym or ranking rule because a case here failed. Fix the general mechanism, or leave it failing and record it.",
    "If a case here is used to guide a change, delete it from this file and write a new one. A holdout consulted twice is not a holdout.",
    "Prompts are deliberately harder than Afro-Bench: heavy pidgin, indirect phrasing, and domains with thin tool vocabulary.",
    "Report the holdout number next to the Afro-Bench number, always. Quoting the tuned score alone is the exact dishonesty this file exists to prevent."
  ],
  "history": [
    {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "version": "afro-1.1",
      "accuracy": "4/10",
      "errorRecall": "5/6",
      "note": "first run; routing generalises poorly, calibration generalises well"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "version": "afro-1.1",
      "note": "expanded to 52 cases; n=10 was too small to support any claim"
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-26",
      "version": "afro-1.1-final",
      "cases": 52,
      "accuracy": "28/52 (54%) vs production 27/52 — routing is NOT the win",
      "wrongAndConfident": "8/24 (33%) vs production 22/25 (88%) — this is the win",
      "note": "n=10 showed 40->50% accuracy; at n=52 that vanished as noise. Expanding the holdout is what made the real result visible."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-07-27",
      "version": "afro-1.2",
      "cases": 52,
      "accuracy": "34/52 (65%) — was 30/52 (58%) at v1.1",
      "precisionWhenConfident": "95% — was 84%",
      "recallOfOwnErrors": "94% — was 86%",
      "note": "Retrieval was NO LONGER the ceiling once synonym expansion landed (never-retrieved 14 -> 3). Ranking became the bottleneck: @5 was 43/52 while @1 was 29/52. Fixes were country scoping across all 54 markets and a blended precision metric."
    }
  ],
